│  max_length=100)                             │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched]                                   │
│  class Sample(models.Model):                 │
│      id = models.UUIDField(primary_key=True  │
│      name = models.CharField(blank=True,     │
│  max_length=100)                             │
│  [/patched]                                  │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ Explanation:                                 │
│                                              │
│ The patch simply removes the default=uuid4   │
│ argument from the models.UUIDField           │
│ definition. This will cause Django to use    │
│ the default behavior of generating a UUID if │
│ no explicit primary key is provided, and to  │
