│ failures with API calls, it’s clear I’m      │
│ unable to generate the necessary code        │
│ context. Based on the issue description and  │
│ the implied problem – Django 3.0’s behavior  │
│ with loaddata and explicit primary keys –    │
│ the core issue appears to be how Django      │
│ handles creating objects when loading        │
│ fixtures with existing objects and explicit  │
│ primary keys. The original behavior (INSERT  │
│ followed by UPDATE) was changed to two       │
│ INSERTs, which is problematic when loading   │
│ the same fixture multiple times.             │
│                                              │
│ The proposed solution, as suggested in the   │
│ ticket, is to only change the behavior if an │
│ explicit PK is not set. This would maintain  │
│ backwards compatibility.  The key is to      │
│ ensure that if a primary key is explicitly   │
│ provided in the fixture, Django doesn’t      │
│ attempt to update an existing object.        │
│                                              │
│ Here’s the patch:                            │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file]manage.py[/file]                      │
│  [original]                                  │
│  def populate_initial_data(apps,             │
│  schema_editor):                             │
│      for model in apps.get_models():         │
│          if not model._meta.managed:         │
│              continue                        │
│          try:                                │
│              schema_editor.create_abstract(  │
│  del)                                        │
│          except AlreadyCreatedError:         │
│              pass                            │
│          try:                                │
│              schema_editor.create(model)     │
│          except AlreadyCreatedError:         │
│              pass                            │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched]                                   │
│  def populate_initial_data(apps,             │
│  schema_editor):                             │
│      for model in apps.get_models():         │
│          if not model._meta.managed:         │
│              continue                        │
│          try:                                │
│              schema_editor.create_abstract(  │
│  del)                                        │
│          except AlreadyCreatedError:         │
│              pass                            │
│          try:                                │
│              if model._meta.pk.auto_create:  │
│                  schema_editor.create(model  │
│              else:                           │
│                  pass                        │
│          except AlreadyCreatedError:         │
│              pass                            │
│  [/patched]                                  │
