│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The first patch modifies the                 │
│ populate_initial_data function in manage.py. │
│ It adds a check to see if the model has an   │
│ auto-created primary key. If it does, it     │
│ proceeds to create the model. Otherwise, it  │
│ skips the creation. This addresses the core  │
│ issue of avoiding duplicate inserts when     │
│ fixtures contain explicit primary keys and   │
