│ in an INSERT followed by an UPDATE. However, │
│ in Django 3.0, it leads to two INSERT        │
│ statements, causing potential data           │
│ duplication. The problem lies within the     │
│ save() method of the Sample model,           │
│ specifically how it handles the primary key  │
│ assignment. The intended behavior is to      │
│ either update an existing row if the pk      │
│ already exists or insert a new row if it     │
│ doesn’t. The current implementation in       │
│ Django 3.0 appears to be incorrectly         │
│ inserting a duplicate row when an explicit   │
│ pk is provided. The Sample model definition  │
│ is missing from the provided context, so we  │
